# Core rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` before architecture-affecting work.
- This product is for offline CS2 demo review.
- Never add DLL injection, game-memory reading/writing, binary patching, wallhack-like overlays, or live competitive assistance.
- Demo-derived facts are authoritative; AI may explain but not invent facts.
- Keep parser access behind `DemoParserAdapter`.
- Keep CS2 console/replay access behind `Cs2ReplayAdapter`.
- Keep capture behind `CaptureAdapter`.
- Keep AI provider access behind `AiProvider`.
- Renderer must not hold provider API keys or analyzer session secrets.
- Long-running work must use persisted cancellable jobs.
- Do not assume a fixed tick rate.
- Every behavior change requires tests.
- Do not bypass typed contracts with ad-hoc dictionaries unless the boundary is explicitly untyped.
